<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Unelli</h1><p class="st-meta">300 BCE – 56 BCE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Gallic people of the Cotentin peninsula whose leader Viridovix headed a coalition against Caesar in 56 BCE.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Unelli held the Cotentin in western <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-normandy">Normandy</a>. Caesar lists them among the Armorican peoples who submitted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/publius-licinius-crassus">Publius Crassus</a> in 57 BCE.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>In 56 BCE their chief <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viridovix">Viridovix</a> commanded a large army of the Unelli, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lexovii">Lexovii</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/aulerci-eburovices">Aulerci Eburovices</a> and others, showing how a war leader could unite several peoples.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quintus-titurius-sabinus">Quintus Titurius Sabinus</a> lured the coalition into attacking his fortified camp uphill and routed it, and the Unelli submitted. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> their chief town moved from Crociatonum to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coutances">Cosedia</a>, renamed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salamis-cyprus">Constantia</a> in late antiquity, the origin of Coutances and of the name Cotentin.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/unelli.jpg" alt="Unelli" width="320" height="320"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Unelli_quater_stater_Gallica_celtiques_884_revers.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>300 BCE – 56 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Viridovix</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gaulish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>France</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Venelli</dd></dl></aside></div>

